{"sections":[],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()"},{"text":" and the store’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"all-or-nothing","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" effect or the imperative "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Identity lives outside the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Choosing an id","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A cancel id is any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to tag the work, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to stop it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Passing ","type":"text"},{"code":"cancelInFlight: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancels any effect already running under the id ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".queryChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from view or scene code"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"What it does not replace"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"text":" continuation should still release it — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"defer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"else","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" has to stop the effect early.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Cancel Effects","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"tit